VIII. Florida Standards Alignment

Mindful Learning Academy courses are designed to align with Florida academic expectations, including Florida’s B.E.S.T. Standards for English Language Arts and Mathematics. Instruction supports mastery, academic progression, college readiness, and measurable student growth.

IX. Assessment and College Readiness Alignment

Mindful Learning Academy uses a mastery-based instructional model supported by internal and external measures of student progress.

Internal assessment includes notebook evidence, lesson checkpoints, lesson quizzes, unit assessments, performance-based tasks, project-based learning artifacts, and revision cycles based on instructor feedback.

External academic progress is measured through a nationally norm-referenced assessment selected by the academy for scholarship compliance, growth monitoring, and instructional planning.

SAT readiness is embedded within English and mathematics coursework. English courses develop reading comprehension, vocabulary in context, grammar, evidence-based reasoning, and writing. Mathematics courses develop algebraic fluency, data analysis, quantitative reasoning, and problem-solving.

X. Mastery-Based Credit Structure

High school credit is awarded based on demonstrated mastery rather than seat time.

Credit is earned through:

Demonstrated mastery of 80% or higher
Performance-based tasks and assessments
Project-based learning artifacts
Structured feedback and revision cycles
Weekly goals and pacing expectations
Time-on-task aligned to course rigor
Completion of required course components and assessments

